{
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "units": "mm",
  "meta": {
    "title": "X Carriage (graph twin)",
    "notes": "Golden twin of main.py (graph format 1.1): the same parameters, the same derivations and the same operations in the same order. main.py stays the oracle; y4d-spec --parity compares the two at the defaults and at every preset. Clamps are min/max pairs spelled as ternaries (toolhead_y first, as the script clamps it first); min/max/sorted of derived values are ternaries; teeth_toward_toolhead is the script's _back = -1 / +1 as a ternary; the two jaw sides (sign +1 / -1) are unrolled. The pockets and posts run along +Y: a z cylinder laid down by rotate x -90 and spun by rotate y -90, which puts the B-rep seam where makeCylinder puts it (x direction +Z). Cited facts as main.py: MGN12H L 45.4, W 27, B 20 x C 20 (HIWIN MG); GT2 2MR belt B 1.52, T 0.76 (Pfeifer 2MR/PGGT2), U 0.254 (SDP/SI Table 4); belt width 6 (guide p. 131); M3 clearance 3.4, counterbore 6.5 x 3.5 (ISO 4762); every other number is a labelled convention of main.py."
  },
  "parameters": {
    "belt_line": {"default": 23.0},
    "belt_a_level": {"default": 38.0},
    "belt_b_level": {"default": 22.0},
    "clamp_x": {"default": 20.0},
    "teeth_toward_toolhead": {"default": false},
    "jaw_length": {"default": 12.0},
    "post_d": {"default": 5.0},
    "slot_w": {"default": 2.4},
    "plate_t": {"default": 8.0},
    "toolhead_y": {"default": 30.0}
  },
  "derived": [
